WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:04.360
Welcome to the Sequencer Modular Framework for Game Development

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.960
course for Unreal Engine 5.5.

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.320
This course is the third video in this series designed

4
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.160
to provide knowledge in Sequencer-based workflows,

5
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.640
specifically building in-game cutscenes for video games.

6
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.839
We'll recap game development principles, Sequencer concepts,

7
00:00:18.839 --> 00:00:21.920
features, and tools of Sequencer,

8
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.039
then dive into migrating level-based logic

9
00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:28.039
into a standalone Blueprint to control in-game cutscenes.

10
00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:30.879
Finally, we'll cover some best practice recommendations

11
00:00:30.879 --> 00:00:34.240
when using Sequencer for game development.

12
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.840
For this course, you'll find the Sequence 305 Start Map located

13
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:44.359
in the Content, Courses, Sequence 305.0.0 Maps folder.

14
00:00:44.359 --> 00:00:45.119
Let's get started.
